  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#obtaining-a-resource-from-a-link-element:parse-a-url\r\n\r\n> Parse the URL given by the href attribute, relative to the element's node document\\. If that fails, then abort these steps\\. Otherwise, let url be the resulting URL record\\.\r\n> \r\n\r\nSee https://github.com/w3c/preload/issues/88\r\n\r\nI think we should fire 'error' event for, at least, stylesheet and preload `link`s. \r\n\r\nAlso these elements: https://github.com/w3c/preload/issues/88#issuecomment-281966790",
